<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells ferro-columbium.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells ferro-columbium.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense National Stockpile Center sold 7,308 pounds of contained columbium in ferro-columbium to Parkans International for an approximate current market value of $44,000.</p>
<p>The awarded material confirms to stockpile grade E which is at least 60 percent columbium and has a columbium to tantalum ratio of at least 8 to 1.</p>
<p>The next sale of ferro-columbium, known as ferro-niobium outside the U.S., is on May 13.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
